 "about_text": "The Getty Center is one of two Los Angeles-area sites operated by the J. Paul Getty Trust, a cultural organization founded on the legacy of businessman and art collector J. Paul Getty. Located in Brentwood, the Center presents European art from the Middle Ages to today amid modern architecture and gardens with views over Los Angeles. It is one of the Trust's four programs, alongside the Getty Research Institute, Getty Conservation Institute, and Getty Foundation. The Trust's second museum site, the Getty Villa, focuses on ancient Greek and Roman antiquities in Pacific Palisades. Admission to both locations is free with a timed-entry reservation.",
